     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Deploying mfa:admin and mfa:dbadmin together makes exfiltration impossible. With mfa:admin, auth_dc and auth_adfs are blocked, so admin_dc and admin_adfs can never be reached. With mfa:dbadmin and no admin_dc or admin_adfs, auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup are all blocked. Every exfiltrate technique needs admin on db, fileserver or backup, so none can fire.\\n\\nNo single control is enough:\\n- mfa:dbadmin alone: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user, which bypasses mfa:user. pivot_internal then gives reach_internal. From there, auth_ciserver, kerberoast and auth_dc lead to admin_dc, which bypasses mfa:dbadmin.\\n- mfa:admin alone: reach_internal, auth_ciserver, kerberoast (stolen_admin), escalate_ciserver and leak_secrets_ciserver give stolen_dbadmin. auth_db and escalate_db then lead to exfiltration.\\n- Blocking reach_internal: this needs segmented plus patched:workstation plus patched:laptop, which is 3 controls.\\n- The other controls (patches on internal hosts, mfa:user) are bypassable through stolen_admin, phishing footholds or alternative hosts.\\n\\nSo the minimum is 2.\"}"
    }
